 34CL    27AL(12C,ANG)                 2014BI03                  ENSDF    202609
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34CL c  2014Bi03: a 40-MeV 12C beam was provided from the 14-UD Pelletron      
 34CL2c  accelerator at the Tata Institute of Fundamental Research, Mumbai. The 
 34CL3c  target was 0.50-mg/cm{+2} {+27}Al on 10-mg/cm{+2} Au backing. States of
 34CL4c  34CL were populated via the {+27}Al({+12}C,|an){+34}Cl heavy-ion       
 34CL5c  reaction and the deexciting |g rays were detected using the Indian     
 34CL6c  National Gamma Array, consisting of 15 Compton-suppressed clover       
 34CL7c  detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO), and integrated 
 34CL8c  polarization asymmetry (IPDCO). Deduced levels, J, |p, |g-ray          
 34CL9c  multipolarities, lifetimes from DSAM lineshape analysis, and transition
 34CLAc  strengths. Comparisons with large-basis shell-model calculations.      
 34CL c  1978Ba39: 27-45-MeV {+12}C beams from the Strasbourg tandem            
 34CL2c  accelerator, France, impinged on 350-|mg/cm{+2} Al targets on Ta       
 34CL3c  backings. |g rays were detected using two Ge(Li) detectors. Measured   
 34CL4c  |g|g-coin and |g|g(|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, |g-ray multipolarities, 
 34CL5c  and lifetimes using the Recoil Distance Method (RDM). Also measured the
 34CL6c  {+31}P(|a,n|g){+34}Cl reaction.                                        
 34CL d  
 34CL cG E,RI$From 2014Bi03, unless otherwise noted. 2014Bi03 provides only     
 34CL2cG statistical uncertainties for I|g in Table I. The systematic           
 34CL3cG uncertainties are |?5%, which arise from the efficiency curve and      
 34CL4cG fittings, as communicated by M. Saha Sarkar in an email reply to B.    
 34CL5cG Singh on February 17, 2014. The evaluators have combined the           
 34CL6cG statistical and systematic uncertainties in quadrature.                
 34CL cG M$From 2014Bi03 based on measured |g|g(|q)(DCO) and |g|g(|q)(POL).     
 34CL2cG R{-DCO}(D) is from gating on a known stretched dipole (|DJ=1)          
 34CL3cG transition and R{-DCO}(Q) is from gating on a known stretched          
 34CL4cG quadrupole (|DJ=2) transition. Expected R{-DCO}(Q)|?1.0 for stretched  
 34CL5cG quadrupole (|DJ=2) or unstretched dipole (|DJ=0) transitions;          
 34CL6cG R{-DCO}(Q)|?0.5 and R{-DCO}(D)|?1.0 for stretched dipole (|DJ=1)       
 34CL7cG transitions. For different multipolarities of the gating and projected 
 34CL8cG transitions, the R{-DCO} value depends on the angle between the        
 34CL9cG detectors and the amount of mixing present in the mixed multipolarity  
 34CLAcG transition. A positive POL indicates an electric character, and a      
 34CLBcG negative POL indicates a magnetic character.                           
 34CL cG TI$2014Bi03 provides only statistical uncertainties for the |g         
 34CL2cG branching ratios in Table II. According to the email reply to B. Singh 
 34CL3cG from the corresponding author M. Saha Sarkar on February 17, 2014, the 
 34CL4cG |g branching ratios listed in Table II of 2014Bi03 were measured       
 34CL5cG separately by gating on transitions above the level. The systematic    
 34CL6cG uncertainties for these measurements are |?5%, which arise from the    
 34CL7cG efficiency curve and fittings. The evaluators have combined the        
 34CL8cG statistical and systematic uncertainties in quadrature. In some cases, 
 34CL9cG the branching ratios differ significantly from those derived from the  
 34CLAcG I|g data in Table I of 2014Bi03. The I|g data in Table I should be     
 34CLBcG considered more reliable, as the authors suggested in their email      
 34CLCcG reply.                                                                 
